# Core Provider Onboarding & Connector Distribution

See task stream `AIPIFY.CORE.PROVIDER.ONBOARDING.CONNECTOR.DISTRIBUTION.V1`.

## Permanent rules

1. **Never assume server access** — customers connect via oauth, api_key_existing_provider, installable_connector, aipify_hosted_connector, or custom_provider_implementation.
2. **Onboarding mode, implementation owner, distribution channel, and install target are required** on every Core onboarding contract.
3. **Core owns the contract** (`app_portal_integration_providers.onboarding_contract`) — APP renders generically.
4. **No provider/customer hardcoding** in shared APP UI — Unonight is an ordinary `api_key_existing_provider` row.
5. **No pilot advantage** and **no custom Unonight APP panel**.
6. **No connector without versioning**; downloads require checksum + signature metadata.
7. **Never execute install commands** from database content — display-only.
8. **No open redirects**; package/docs/OAuth URLs must pass allowlist validation.
9. **No secrets in metadata or URLs**.
10. **Tenant / provider / installation exact** — no first-row fallback.
11. **State machine enforced** — no `active` before `verified`; no `active` when blocked/unsupported.
12. **i18n required** for modes, support, readiness, responsibilities, and states.
13. **Premium responsive design** required for onboarding surfaces.
14. Full e2e customer integration readiness is separate from Core onboarding/distribution Production Ready.
15. **One invalid provider must not crash the Platform route** (`/platform/provider-onboarding`).
16. **Partial failure is isolated per provider** — invalid contracts render a blocker card; valid providers still render.
17. **Security-critical fields remain fail-closed** (mode, scopes, URLs, secrets, package checksum/signature).
18. **Non-critical display fields may use safe fallback** — never hide security/data corruption.
19. **Never pass functions from Server Components into Client Components** — use serializable `messageCatalog` / labels only (RSC digest `340189304` class).
20. **Authenticated Production route verification is required** before Production Ready.
21. **No Production Ready from build/Preview alone** — manual live route proof on `app.aipify.ai` is mandatory.
22. **Structured Platform editor is primary** — typed sections for contract administration.
23. **Raw JSON is advanced secondary only** — accordion/tab with validation; never the default work surface.
24. **No raw enum/status in UI** — localize modes, readiness, support, states, owners, channels, targets.
25. **No English leakage** in non-English locales for onboarding/admin copy.
26. **Reference fixtures must be labeled** — never presented as live production providers.
27. **Unavailable is not the same as invalid** — missing contract ≠ malformed contract.
28. **Provider key is secondary technical metadata** — display name is primary.
29. **All contract editing requires validation / version / audit**.
30. **Preview must use the same generic APP renderer** (`ProviderOnboardingOverview`).
31. **Premium desktop / mobile / dark design** is required for Platform provider onboarding.

## Forbidden

- Parallel provider registries or local JSON as source of truth
- `if (provider === "unonight")` in shared APP presentation
- Arbitrary shell execution or unvalidated install command rendering
- Unsafe file hosting without checksum/signature metadata
- Mixing vault/secret encryption changes into onboarding contract work
- Declaring Production Ready without authenticated live `/platform/provider-onboarding` proof
- Letting a single bad provider contract crash the entire Platform page
- Treating reference fixtures or missing contracts as identical to parse failures
- Making raw JSON the primary Platform admin surface
